    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8420" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεπί-σκεπτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>inattentive, inconsiderate,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρᾶγμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					5.143
				</span></i>
			 C.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλογία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Abst.</u>
					1.43
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁρμή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Procop.
					<u>Goth.</u>
					4.32
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.45
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἔχειν τινός</span> to give
				<i>no consideration</i> to . ., <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>GA</u>
				778b10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>not examined, unregarded,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				2.4.3
			</span></i>; <i>unobserved,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Anon.
				<u>in SE</u>
				12.27
			</span></i>.</div>
